/-!
# Paper A (lock v12), lane `owner:a-eth-7`, segment 6c: the square decider realises the square route-B identity

Text of the frozen a-eth-owner-6 module `E6Join` from `decAlg` to `decAlg_join` (generated by `make_sqjoin.py`),
with the machine, clock and cutoff of `E7SqDec` (`decMachineSq`, `decTimeSq`, `N0Sq`), the square header word
(`hwOfSq`, `hwLenSq`, `hw_length_eq_sq`) and, on the law side, the a-eth-owner-2 square header word
`Paper2.AEth2.headerWordSq` (module `E2Sq`) and square identity `Paper2.AEth2.JoinRealisesSq`; the two transport
lemmas `hw_transport_sq`, `len_transport_sq` below replace `hw_transport`, `len_transport`. The generic
`Paper2.AEth5.vecOf`, `ofFn_vecOf`, `split_law` are reused by exact name.

* `decAlgSq`: the R20 carrier algorithm (same computed tape length `tapeCA (phiLen N₁) (7 + C.cR)`, same length
  machine and `lenPoly` as `Paper2.AEth5.decAlg`), machine `decMachineSq`, clock `decTimeSq`, output DEFINED as
  what the machine prints at its clock.
* `decAlgSq_joinAt`: on EVERY word `x`, the square identity at the routed formula; `decAlgSq_join`: at
  `x = encode Φ` for `K`-sparse valid `Φ` with `N₁ ≤ N`, `Paper2.AEth2.JoinRealisesSq D B Φ (kOf N) E`.

No ledger row is closed. Nothing here is admitted.
-/

